          "message": {
            "text": "Projective activation is based on geometry, not on matrix3d syntax. The fourth-corner identity q2 = q1 + q3 - q0 separates affine planes that SVG can keep as vectors from genuinely projective quads; an authored perspective context also activates the boundary because its descendant flattening and depth composition cannot be represented by SVG groups.",
            "markdown": "Projective activation is based on geometry, not on matrix3d syntax. The fourth-corner identity q2 = q1 + q3 - q0 separates affine planes that SVG can keep as vectors from genuinely projective quads; an authored perspective context also activates the boundary because its descendant flattening and depth composition cannot be represented by SVG groups."
          },
          "locations": [
